course: dictionary
lesson: 10636
title: Unheard and unheard of
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unheard has two meanings. The first is not heard by anyone, or not listened to. «Her cries for help went unheard in the storm.» Nobody could hear her over the wind, so her cries were unheard.
explain: The second meaning is in the phrase unheard of. It means never known or done before, very unusual. «Shark attacks are very rare everywhere and almost unheard of around Britain.» This does not mean nobody has ever heard of sharks. It means such attacks are so rare that people hardly ever hear of them.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, read the words around it. If people are not listening, it is the first meaning. If the sentence is about something rare or new, it is the second. Then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Unheard means not heard by anyone, or not listened to.
fact: Unheard of means never known or done before, very unusual.
fact: The prefix un- often means not, so unheard means not heard.
fact: Useful phrases: go unheard, voices unheard, and unheard of.
fact: «Whether a tree falling unheard makes a sound depends on the meaning of "sound".» This shows that the word sound can mean different things in different sentences.
exercise: «Her cries for help went unheard in the storm.» What does unheard mean here? | Sung in a song | Written down on paper | *Not heard by anyone | Very loud and clear
exercise: «Shark attacks are almost unheard of around Britain.» What does unheard of mean? | Very quiet and small | *Never known or done before, very unusual | Heard by everyone in the town | Easy to spot at the beach
exercise: Copy the word that means not listened to: «Some people felt unheard.» | *unheard | felt | people | some
test: «The villagers' pleas went unheard by the council for years.» What does unheard mean here? | Written in a book | *Not listened to | Sung at a village fair | Loud and clear
test: Which phrase means very unusual, never done before? | *unheard of | voices unheard | go unheard | unheard tree
exam: «Walking on the Moon was unheard of until the 1960s.» What does unheard of mean in this sentence? | *Never known or done before, very unusual | Heard by everyone on the news | Very quiet and hard to hear | Not listened to by the scientists
